= Abstract

#chapter-kicker([Why this demo matters], 
[This project shows how Typst can structure a computational structural engineering thesis instead of treating it like a manually formatted word-processor file.])

This sandbox uses *EtabExtension* as the running case study. The thesis topic is practical: structural engineers typically work with binary `.edb` files, but reviewing alternatives, tracking changes, and producing repeatable reports is difficult when comparison depends on manual screenshots and ad hoc spreadsheets.

The document demonstrates a Typst workflow with reusable styling, split chapters, external figures, data-driven tables, bibliography handling, and small helper functions. The technical case study itself is inspired by version-control ideas in software engineering @spinellis.

*Keywords:* Typst, ETABS, structural engineering, reproducible reporting, computational workflow.
